# # You tried to fix:

# # 🔸 Q10 (entity issue)
# # 🔸 Q11 (trivial answer)

# # But your fixes were:

# # Fix	Type
# # semantic threshold	⚠️ partial
# # trivial filter	⚠️ detection only
# # 🔥 Why they still fail
# # 🔴 Q10 — still wrong entity

# # You added something like:

# # if semantic_score < threshold:
# #     reject

# # 👉 Problem:

# # This filters bad answers

# # BUT does NOT:

# # ❗ choose the BEST answer

# # So system still:

# # picks 1 candidate
# # never compares alternatives

# # 👉 That’s why:

# # ❌ Wrong person still selected

# # 🔴 Q11 — trivial answer

# # You detect:

# # trivial answer filter triggered

# # BUT from your log:

# # → still accepted
# # → then empty safety net
# # → FAIL

# # 👉 That means:

# # ❗ You detect but DO NOT enforce rejection
# # Fix 1 (Q11) — Both trivial answer blocks now do a hard return state with "This information is not present in the document." and decision_type = "rejected_trivial" instead of just blanking answer = "" (which was falling through and hitting the empty answer safety net incorrectly).
# # Fix 2 (Q10) — Added the ambiguity guard block above the kw_r > 0.7 tier in the ReAct decision chain. It fires only when semantic similarity is very low (< 0.3) but keyword overlap is suspiciously high (> 0.8) — the pattern of wrong entity selection where a name appears in context but isn't actually the right answer.


