# # works but got soft hallucinations & got wrong confidence score display somewhere it is getting divied twice nd another issue got is thaat  that wehn i asked what is the name of lecture 3 it gave me wrong answwer 
# # Clear problem. RoBERTa extracted "Data Source Regulator" with score 0.7757 — which passes should_use_roberta (score >= 0.4). But it's a wrong answer.
# # The issue is RoBERTa is extractive — it finds the highest-scoring span in any retrieved chunk, regardless of whether that chunk actually contains the lecture name. "Data Source Regulator" appears in some other chunk that scored high due to the number "3" matching other things.
# # Two separate problems here:
# # Problem 1 — RoBERTa bypasses verification entirely. RoBERTa answers are accepted directly with verified=True, kw_score=1.0 hardcoded — no actual verification runs on them. This was a design assumption that "extractive = always correct" which is wrong.
# # Problem 2 — Retrieval score is 24.4% but RoBERTa still answers. The hard rejection gate only runs before RoBERTa. If retrieval is low and RoBERTa gives a confident-looking answer, it slips through.
# # The fix: Run RoBERTa answers through verification too, specifically when retrieval_score is low. If retrieval_score < 30 and RoBERTa answers, still verify it before accepting.






