# # 💥 LLM interpretation:
# # tweeted ≠ said (exact wording mismatch)
# # → NOT explicitly supported
# # → NO ❌
# # ⚠️ Even though logically:
# # tweeted = said ✔️
# # 🔥 THIS IS THE EXACT FAILURE

# # ❗ Your verifier is doing string-level strictness instead of semantic matching

