# # got not in the pdf but it is being retrived but the because of the score it is going to NO
# Good — this is not a bug, but it is a configuration mistake you introduced while fixing hallucinations.

# Let’s break it clearly 👇

# 🧠 What’s happening right now

# Your system says:

# 🚫 Retrieval score 19.9% < 25% — hard reject

# 👉 So it never even tries to answer

# 🔥 But here’s the contradiction

# You ALSO have:

# Recall@6 = 100% ✅

# 👉 Meaning:

# The correct chunk IS already retrieved

# 💥 So the real problem is:

# ❗ Your retrieval_score calculation is wrong / too harsh

# 🧠 Why this happens (VERY IMPORTANT)

# Your current score:

# retrieval_score = mean cosine similarity
# Problem with mean:

# You retrieved:

# 1 very relevant chunk (correct answer) ✅
# 5 weak/noisy chunks ❌

# 👉 Mean becomes low:

# (0.8 + 0.2 + 0.1 + 0.1 + 0.1 + 0.1)/6 ≈ 0.23 → 23%

# 👉 So:

# system thinks → "bad retrieval"
# ⚠️ But reality is:

# ❗ You already have the correct chunk

# 🔥 ROOT CAUSE

# ❗ You are using mean similarity instead of max similarity

# ✅ FINAL FIX (THIS WILL SOLVE YOUR ISSUE)
# 🔧 Change retrieval score calculation
# ❌ CURRENT:
# return np.mean(sims) * 100
# ✅ FIX:
# return np.max(sims) * 100
# 🧠 Why this works

# Now:

# max similarity = 0.8 → 80%

# 👉 System correctly understands:

# “I HAVE a strong match”

# 🚀 What happens after fix
# Your case:
# BEFORE:
# retrieval_score = 19% → reject ❌
# AFTER:
# retrieval_score = 80% → proceed ✅
# 🔥 THIS IS THE KEY INSIGHT
# Metric	Meaning
# Mean similarity	overall quality (bad for gating)
